{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>From his flesh.</b> The tradition has already established: ״from his flesh״ and not on account of compulsion — meaning that the zav emits fluid on account of his flesh, which is a designation for the membrum or the seminal vessel, and not on account of another cause that expels the flux. And the Sages, of blessed memory, already explained (Niddah 35b) that the flux is like the white of a fertile egg. And when this occurs מִבְּשָׂרוֹ — that is, on account of disease of the seminal vessel alone — this indicates their weakness and failure of digestion, which befalls the majority on account of excessive frequency of intercourse and its concomitant imaginings, wherein the impulse of folly's sin does not cease. It is therefore fitting that he count seven clean days, through which his imaginings will depart from his heart, and immerse from the impurity, and make atonement with a sin-offering and a burnt-offering for what he did and imagined."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:22.732584757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}